 Office premium calculation and claim processing\n**Test File**: src/claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 35\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. should compute premium for empty item list as 5 G -- processing fee only\n2. should compute 100 G base premium for a sword\n3. should compute 60 G base premium for an amulet\n4. should compute 80 G base premium for a staff\n5. should compute 40 G base premium for a potion\n6. should compute 25 G base premium per component (rune or moonstone)\n7. should apply 60 G special base premium for a block of exactly 3 alike components\n8. should not apply block discount for 2 runes -- expect 50 G\n9. should apply block discount for 3 runes -- expect 60 G\n10. should not apply block discount for 4 runes -- expect 100 G\n11. should compute 175 G base premium for 7 runes\n12. should not form block with 2 runes + 1 moonstone -- expect 75 G\n13. should form two separate blocks with 3 runes + 3 moonstones -- expect 120 G\n14. should add 50% risk surcharge for cursed items\n15. should add 30% risk surcharge for highly enchanted items (enchantment level ≥ 5)\n16. should apply 20% loyalty discount for customers with ≥ 2 years with MHPCO\n17. should add 10% initial assessment surcharge for first insurance\n18. should apply 15% discount on each contract after the first\n19. should compute 165 G premium for newcomer with cursed sword -- 100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\n20. should compute 160 G premium for long-standing customer's second contract with cursed, highly enchanted sword -- includes both first insurance surcharge and follow-up discount\n21. should apply cursed surcharge only to the cursed sword's base premium in a policy with cursed sword and plain amulet -- total base 160 G, surcharge 50 G\n22. should round premium of 197.5 G up to 198 G in MHPCO's favor\n23. should round payout of 350.5 G down to 350 G in MHPCO's favor\n24. should apply 100 G deductible per damage event\n25. should cap total payout per policy at twice the insurance sum\n26. should reimburse 400 G for regular sword (steel, enchantment 3) with 500 G damage -- full minus 100 G deductible\n27. should reimburse 100 G for rune with 200 G damage -- full minus 100 G deductible\n28. should reimburse 400 G for dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, 1000 G damage -- 50% rule wins, then deductible\n29. should reimburse 700 G for dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, 800 G damage -- dragon-material clause applies\n30. should reimburse 400 G for steel sword, enchantment 9, 1000 G damage -- high-enchantment clause applies\n31. should support policy with two swords -- insurance sum 2000 G, cap 4000 G\n32. should apply separate 100 G deductible for each damaged sword in dragon attack\n33. should reject claim when damages array contains more entries of a type than insured -- exit with non-zero status\n34. should have 600 G payout and 0 G remaining cap for second claim of 1500 G when cap was already reduced to 600 G\n35. should exit with non-zero status code when quote includes an item with unknown type\n36. should exit with non-zero status code when claim references a damage entry whose item is not part of the policy\n37. should exit with non-zero status code when"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784951282729,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-1a31046e-3ddd-4a45-8ffe-54f0532971e3","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"}}
