0 G in MHPCO's favor\n24. should apply 100 G deductible per damage event\n25. should cap total payout per policy at twice the insurance sum\n26. should reimburse 400 G for regular sword (steel, enchantment 3) with 500 G damage -- full minus 100 G deductible\n27. should reimburse 100 G for rune with 200 G damage -- full minus 100 G deductible\n28. should reimburse 400 G for dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, 1000 G damage -- 50% rule wins, then deductible\n29. should reimburse 700 G for dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, 800 G damage -- dragon-material clause applies\n30. should reimburse 400 G for steel sword, enchantment 9, 1000 G damage -- high-enchantment clause applies\n31. should support policy with two swords -- insurance sum 2000 G, cap 4000 G\n32. should apply separate 100 G deductible for each damaged sword in dragon attack\n33. should reject claim when damages array contains more entries of a type than insured -- exit with non-zero status\n34. should have 600 G payout and 0 G remaining cap for second claim of 1500 G when cap was already reduced to 600 G\n35. should exit with non-zero status code when quote includes an item with unknown type\n36. should exit with non-zero status code when claim references a damage entry whose item is not part of the policy\n37. should exit with non-zero status code when claim contains a damage entry with negative amount\n\nTest List Phase Complete. Proceeding to Red phase with the first test."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784951282729,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-1a31046e-3ddd-4a45-8ffe-54f0532971e3","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"}}
